# DWT quality checklist

- [ ] Follows the existing version / section / page pattern, and any new version has an index card and a `versions/vN.html` page
- [ ] Extends the right layout for its version and sets `version`, `pageName` and `activeSection`; links are built from `version`, not hard-coded
- [ ] Accessibility met: WCAG 2.2 AA, labelled inputs, `govukErrorSummary` pattern, `aria-live` for dynamic feedback, and the journey works without JavaScript
- [ ] GOV.UK Design System components used via macros, with custom styles only as `app-*` classes in `application.scss`
- [ ] New/edited content follows the GOV.UK style guide, without silently rewriting untouched existing content
- [ ] New form data handled on the server in `routes.js` and held in version-specific session data, with synthetic data only
- [ ] New routes added inside the right version's `registerVNRoutes()`, under the relevant section banner
- [ ] The version page records what changed and why
- [ ] Nothing existing renamed, moved, or restructured without being asked
